==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|knotty}}, {{m|enm|knotti}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|knot|y|id2=adjectival}}. Compare {{cog|nl|knoestig|t=knotty}}, {{cog|de|knotig|t=knotty}}, {{cog|sv|knutig}}, {{m|sv|knotig|t=knotty}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-knotty.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{homophones|en|naughty}} {{qualifier|in accents with the [[w:cot-caught merger|cot-caught merger]]}}
:* {{rhymes|en|ɒti}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er|more}}

# Full of [[knot]]s.
#: '''''knotty''' pine''
#* '''1610-11''', [[w:William Shakespeare|William Shakespeare]], ''[[w:The Tempest|The Tempest]]'', Act I Scene 2
#*: If thou murmur'st, I will rend an oak
#*: And [[peg]] thee in his '''knotty''' entrails till
#*: Thou hast howl'd away twelve winters.
# [[complicated|Complicated]] or [[tricky]]; [[complex]]; [[difficult]].
#: {{synonyms|en|intricate|thorny}}
#: ''a '''knotty''' problem''

